window.STATE_PAST_NOTES = {"Maryland":"From the Maryland State Board of Elections' official turnout by party and county (eligible voters and ballots cast). Maryland doesn't break turnout down by age, race or sex.","Kentucky":"From the Kentucky State Board of Elections' turnout reports by age, sex and party (it labels them unofficial). Kentucky's youngest group includes 17-year-olds registered to vote at 18.","South Carolina":"From South Carolina's voter registration system (VREMS) statistics, which count voters by race, sex and age within each county. South Carolina has no party registration. Registered counts every voter on its rolls, so rates can run below turnout figures quoted using active voters only.","California":"From UC Berkeley's Statewide Database, built from county voter files. Its vote history matches about 97% of ballots counted (2024: 15.6 million of 16.1 million certified), so rates run about 2 points low. Latino and Asian voters are identified by surname, an estimate."};
